          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="i46__r1__c1" value="[FIXED] The CPU only configures and starts. The controller then owns the schedule: for each chunk it issues one 1D request (address, length, destination) to the read-only DMA, waits for its completion, starts the GEMM core on the loaded chunk, and moves on (v0 sequential: no overlap of load and compute). Weights Wq, Wk, Wv are 768 x 768 each and arrive in three 768 x 256 chunks, one chunk filling exactly one bram_pp bank. Weights are never written back to DRAM." style="shape=partialRectangle;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;connectable=0;fillColor=none;strokeColor=#000000;strokeWidth=1;overflow=hidden;pointerEvents=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacing=4;fontSize=18;fontColor=#000000;" vertex="1" parent="i46__r1" vlsit_native_table="1">
          <mxGeometry x="330" width="1480" height="102" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle width="1480" height="102" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
