        <mxCell id="i26__r1__c1" value="[EXISTS, Minh] INT8 tile GEMM with TILE = 32. The load controller walks the loops n, m, k, row and reads one A word and one B word per cycle (one 256-bit word = one 32-element tile row); the PE array forms the outer product of a tile pair in 32 cycles; the accumulator sums the k partial tiles of one output tile. The three stages overlap at about 33 cycles per tile pair. In this architecture the B operand comes from bram_pp instead of the original internal B_bram." style="shape=partialRectangle;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;connectable=0;fillColor=none;strokeColor=#000000;strokeWidth=1;overflow=hidden;pointerEvents=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacing=4;fontSize=18;fontColor=#000000;" vertex="1" parent="i26__r1" vlsit_native_table="1">
          <mxGeometry x="330" width="1480" height="102" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle width="1480" height="102" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
